Adding Columns of various types
===============================
- Column 0 of type Double with role X, filled with [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
- Column 1 of type Int, filled with [5, 6, 7]
- Column 2 of type String, filled with ['foo', 'bar', 'baz']
- Column 3 of type Bool, filled with [True, False, True]
- Column 4 of type Double, with 5 versions and role F, filled with 3.0
The Data Base contains 5 column(s) of 3 samples
Column 0/5 : VD (Type: Double) {Role: x1}
Column 1/5 : VI (Type: Id) {Role: NA}
Column 2/5 : VS (Type: String) {Role: z1}
Column 3/5 : VB (Type: Char) {Role: NA}
Column 4/5 : VDS [5] (Type: Double) {Role: f1}

Various ways to specify a column (e.g. for retreiving its name):
================================================================
- by Name : VD
- by Name and Version : VDS
- by Index :  VDS
- by Index and Version : VDS

Various ways to specify a column (e.g. for retreiving its name):
================================================================
- by Name : VD
- by Name and Version : VDS
- by Index : VDS
- by Index and Version : VDS
- by RoleID and Version : VDS
- by Role : VS
- by Role and Index : VS
- by Role and Index and Version : VS

